It is Saturday morning and the café is full.
I am working together with Elif behind the counter.
We are a great team by now.
She prepares the drinks and I serve the customers.
A man comes to the till.
"Good morning, I would like two bread rolls, please," he says.
I pack the bread rolls into a paper bag.
"With pleasure."
"Would you also like something to drink?" I ask him.
"Yes, a coffee, please," the man answers.
Elif makes the drink and hands me the cup.
"Here is the coffee," I say smiling to the man.
"That makes four euros altogether, please."
The customer pays quickly with his card.
"Do you need the till receipt?" I ask politely.
"No, thank you," he says and goes to his table.
The routine behind the till is completely normal for me now.
The short conversations with the customers run smoothly.
"You are doing that really great, Maya," Elif says in a quiet minute.
"Thank you, the shift is fun for me," I answer.
But we cannot talk for long, because the next customer is already waiting.
